 him that said unto him,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#The Lord sware and will not repent,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textºThou art a priest for ever¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ After the order of Melchisedec:)¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9By so much was Jesus made a surety of a better testament.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book9§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And they truly were many priests, because they were not suffered to continue by reason of death:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJbut this man, because he continueth ever, hath an unchangeable priesthood.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto God by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book9§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}For such an high priest became us, who is holy, harmless, undefiled, separate from sinners, and made higher than the heavens;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©who needeth not daily, as those high priests, to offer up sacrifice, first for his own sins, and then for the people's: for this he did once, when he offered up himself.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor the law maketh men high priests which have infirmity; but the word of the oath, which was since the law, maketh the Son, who is consecrated for evermore.¦layout ªlast_verse